WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Today we explore the warm and expressive world of Russian feelings, so you can share exactly how you feel in any moment. I'm Olya, and this is Привет, Русский, episode 71. Our word of the day is rad, rad. It means glad or happy, like when you feel ready to smile. Say it slowly with me, rad. It sounds like the start of radiant, and when you are rad, your face lights up. Listen to this simple sentence.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.940
Я рад видеть тебя.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.380
Дотминтс, я рад to see you.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.880
Now repeat after me.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:36.500
Рад.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.100
With that word in mind, let's add more feelings you can use right away.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.900
Грусный means sad.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:43.800
Грусный.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.080
Say it with me.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:45.820
Грусный.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.780
Next comes злой, which means angry.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:49.480
Злой.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.240
Now we have устал.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:52.620
That means tired.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.040
When a boy or man says it, устал.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.840
A girl would say устала, устала.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.620
Это вождь, к коннекту.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.920
После угредения, когда вы можете

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.140
перебирать нормально.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.220
Это значит хорошо или хорошо.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.340
То есть все хорошо.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.280
Это значит, что всё хорошо.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.500
Сейчас, как вы знаете, что она находится вне,

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.420
у нас есть один стрелок.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.120
Я же это это делаю в раше.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.040
Ладно, в раше, как как раше,

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.600
то, что вы вы знаете, как вы его знаете,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.960
без экстраворбов.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.360
Рашензов often drop the word for is or am.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.640
You just say the feeling and it works.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.840
Own rad means he is glad.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.740
Я устал, means I am tired if you are speaking as a boy.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.500
You can now say a full feeling in Russian with almost no extra words.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:45.340
Short form adjectives in Russian, let you say how someone feels right now without extra

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:45.720
words.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.840
They change slightly for gender.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:53.760
Рад works for he. Рада works for she. They stay simple and daily use.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.980
You drop the work to be entirely in these cases.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.020
Rations just say the feeling word and it is understood right away.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.800
This pattern appears often in spoken Russian. It keeps sentences short and natural.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.880
In everyday Russian chats, people answer the question как дела?

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.800
Which means how are things with one short feeling word such as normal or все хорошо?

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.920
It keeps the talk warm and direct, the way friends share moments across Russia.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.820
People choose these answers to stay friendly.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:28.780
The replies fit many situations without long explanations.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.480
This habit shows up in family talks and with neighbors.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.900
It matches the open style of Russian conversations.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.260
Before we finish, something really cool about one of today's words.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:45.440
Rud traces back to an old route that also gave English the word ready.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:52.200
Лong goal it meant prepared and eager, so when you say Yarat, you are saying you are ready

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.580
and happy to see someone.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.420
It looks a little like the name Rad, but has no link to radiation at all.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:04.100
Picture yourself already ready with a big smile every time you feel Rad, and the word

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.100
will stay with you.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.040
The proto-slavic form Rad connects to the same Indo-European source.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.380
That source also produced the English word Rad.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:13.580
Райд.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.700
The old sense was being prepared and willing.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.560
This link helps the world's ticking memory.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:24.780
The false friend moment with radiation adds a quick reminder to focus on the happy

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:25.720
meaning instead.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.140
Do you remember what rad means?

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:34.860
Try drawing a face for rad, for grussney and for zloy, then write the Russian word under

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:35.400
each one.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:41.700
Or greet a friend today by asking, Hakhdila, and answer with Yarat or Yau-style.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.020
And that's our lesson for today.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.060
Молодец for sticking with it.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.320
Try using today's words in one real sentence before the next episode.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:54.500
Little steps, big progress, poker friends, that's by.

